  "title": "Florida Leprosy Cases Increase: Symptoms, Causes, Prevention, and What You Should Know",
  "summary": "Leprosy, also known as Hansen's disease, is once again making headlines after health officials reported an increase in cases across Florida. Although the disease is considered rare in the United States, recent data has raised public interest and prompted experts to remind people about the symptoms, transmission, and prevention of this ancient bacterial infection. Despite its long history and the stigma often associated with it, leprosy is now a treatable disease when diagnosed early. Understand",
